$ satlink --help info
exit status 0
--- stdout
Talk to an Iridium satellite handset over USB

Usage: satlink [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list     List connected handsets
  info     Manufacturer, model, firmware and IMEI
  status   Signal strength, battery and network registration
  sms      SMS operations
  dial     Place a voice call
  answer   Answer an incoming call
  hangup   End the current call
  at       Send a raw AT command, e.g. `satlink at AT+CSQ`
  monitor  Print unsolicited events (incoming SMS, RING, ...) until interrupted
  net      Use a data call as an IP link that only this program can use
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -p, --port <PORT>
          Serial device (auto-detected by USB vendor ID when omitted)
          
          [env: SATLINK_PORT=]

  -b, --baud <BAUD>
          [default: 19200]

      --simulate[=<SIMULATE>]
          Use a simulated handset instead of a real one, with Iridium's real timing (the default) or instant responses

          Possible values:
          - iridium: Call setup, latency and throughput as measured on Iridium
          - instant: No delays: for quick experiments

  -v, --verbose...
          Log what the link is doing (-v), in more detail (-vv, -vvv)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
--- stderr
